course: dictionary
lesson: 5266
title: One word, many journeys
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A journey is a trip from one place to another, often a long one. You can often find its meaning from the clues around it, such as words about distance, time, or travel. «Long journeys between homes are tiring» tells you the word is about travel, and tiring tells you it takes a lot out of you.
explain: Journey can also mean a long time of change or learning. «Her journey to become a doctor» is not a trip on a bus: it is the whole path of study and work she follows to reach her goal. Try swapping in a simpler word, such as path or trip, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Journey can be a verb too. To journey means to travel, and you will often see it in stories or formal writing. «The explorers journeyed across the frozen land» means the explorers travelled across the frozen land. Check it by swapping in travelled: if the meaning stays the same, you have found it.
fact: A journey is a trip from one place to another, often a long one.
fact: «Commuting» is the daily journey to and from work.
fact: Journey can also mean a long time of change or learning, as in «her journey to become a doctor».
fact: To journey means to travel, often in stories or formal writing.
fact: «The whole journey of a meal through the gut usually takes about one to three days.»
exercise: «Plankton swim up to the surface at night and sink by day, the biggest daily journey of animals on Earth.» What does journey mean here? | A type of plankton | A hungry fish | A bath in the sea | *A regular trip up and down through the water
exercise: «Her journey to become a doctor was long and hard.» What does journey mean here? | *A long time of change and learning | A trip on a train | A short walk to school | A holiday abroad
exercise: «The explorers journeyed across the frozen land for weeks.» What does journeyed mean? | Shouted | *Travelled | Stopped | Slept
test:
«Long journeys between homes are tiring.» Which word tells you the journeys take a lot out of people? | *Tiring | Long | Homes | Between | Journeys are a kind of trip, so they are a type of travel. Choose the word that shows the effect. | *Tiring
test:
«Commuting is the daily journey to and from work.» What does commuting mean? | A yearly holiday by plane | *Travelling to and from work every day | Cooking dinner for the family | Reading a long story
exam: «The whole journey of a meal through the gut usually takes about one to three days.» What does journey mean here? | A holiday on a ship | A tiny fish | A type of food | *The whole path the food takes through the body
